rences. Since both lotteries yield the same sum of pairwise differences (12,000), the reason would be indifferent. But the reason is defined to prefer one or be indifferent. Thus, the reason can be applied, but it does not distinguish between the lotteries in this case. The key point is that the sum of pairwise differences is identical for both lotteries, so the reason cannot prefer one over the other based on this rule.",
